## Lessons

# Principle of Least Privilege
- Users should only have the minimum access needed to do their job
- Reducing excessive permissions minimizes security risks
- Group-based access makes management scalable

# Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)
- Assign permissions to groups, not individual users
- Makes onboarding/offboarding easier (just add/remove from group)
- Clear separation of duties between roles




